{% set local_problem %}
<p>Decatur's river location creates the perfect conditions for fascia damage — and we see it constantly when inspecting homes here. The Tennessee River keeps humidity levels higher in Decatur than areas just a short drive inland. That constantly moist air surrounds your home 365 days a year, and exposed wood pays the price.</p>

<p>Here's what happens: your gutters clog or overflow during a storm. Water runs behind the gutter and soaks into the fascia board. In a drier climate, that wood might dry out within a day or two. In Decatur's humid air, it stays damp much longer — sometimes never fully drying between rain events during wet seasons. That persistent moisture is exactly what rot fungus needs to thrive.</p>

<p>We see fascia damage across every Decatur neighborhood. Historic homes in Albany and downtown often have original wood fascia that's weathered decades of river-town humidity. Mid-century homes throughout the city frequently have fascia that's been repaired multiple times over the years. Even newer construction in Southwest Decatur shows accelerated wear compared to homes in drier areas.</p>

<p>The damage often goes unnoticed until it's extensive. Fascia boards are behind your gutters, out of sight. Paint may look fine from the ground while the wood underneath is rotting through. Many homeowners only discover the problem when gutters start sagging or pulling away from the house.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>We start with a thorough inspection — checking fascia and soffit for water damage, soft spots, and rot. In Decatur's humid environment, we pay special attention to areas where the damage may not be visible: behind gutter brackets, at corners where water tends to collect, and where fascia meets soffit.</p>

<p>For damaged sections, we carefully remove existing gutters, cut out the rotted wood back to solid material, and install new fascia boards. Given Decatur's humidity challenges, we typically recommend moisture-resistant materials: composite boards, treated lumber, or PVC-wrapped options that stand up better to your river-town climate.</p>

<p>Everything is properly sealed, caulked, and prepared for new gutter installation. We use primers and sealants designed for humid conditions, not generic products that break down quickly in moisture-heavy environments.</p>

<p>Then we install your new seamless gutters on the fresh fascia — properly attached with appropriate hangers, properly sloped for drainage, and designed to prevent the overflow that caused the rot in the first place. You get a complete solution from one contractor: carpentry, gutters, and the peace of mind that comes from knowing the job was done right for Decatur's conditions.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been repairing fascia and installing gutters throughout Morgan County for over 20 years. We understand that these two jobs are inseparable — you can't have reliable gutters without solid fascia to mount them on, and you can't protect fascia without properly functioning gutters keeping water away from it.</p>

<p>We also understand what Decatur's humidity does to exposed wood. Our material recommendations, installation techniques, and attention to moisture management are specifically designed for river-town conditions — not generic solutions from a franchise playbook.</p>

<p>Our crews handle both carpentry and gutter installation, which means better coordination, cleaner work, and a single point of accountability. When we're done, your home is fully protected from roof edge to foundation — backed by our warranty and our reputation in Morgan County.</p>
